{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd1930638e05b2b7561088ad7bebf4c648d8298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is a prime number, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48a22b692678034476d0bb61e7a19fc6c51c102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> without remainder \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e5054ca51b5b07469e81d9f1f6d5fb0734a6cf14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{never} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{sometimes only} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{always} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"367\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f6085068158ddc4f2450f17dd559701e26e0a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{only if } p =5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"290\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Starting with some experimentation, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9744b986a275413b1d5e52af4ee4642253f606d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb5a1402e5a2040d6bf90ffcbcdf8a62633c8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.  For these primes, the resulting numbers are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To show that all primes we devise the following proof:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0129347fb90ed68017dcf8a5c405308662914c24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Proof:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cefc51f5aea7c080b1d68bb59b55997d42985c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6dfb3e58443ef161f9daccd660a12135ef457c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> being a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can use modular arithmetic.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6af926c7a457b2284fb9bd782d0fd53b14d386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 - 1 = (p+1)(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fe8d899de32378979bd8628b8bef950cc124af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 \\equiv 0,1,2,3 \\mod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48a22b692678034476d0bb61e7a19fc6c51c102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec471406dec3a0e9fab6d50d105aa6f90fa593a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 \\equiv 0,1,2 \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48a22b692678034476d0bb61e7a19fc6c51c102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6dfb3e58443ef161f9daccd660a12135ef457c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can try a few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cefc51f5aea7c080b1d68bb59b55997d42985c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7ad95040612ce4b4e0c9e4d0ea350b098e36e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9d32dda15520024ae3657763552a86f56da239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\textbf{C})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" /> always divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The proof is as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9257065937c4e8a52ba73ad362ae36998aa4c860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2-1=(p+1)(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"21\" /> and since all primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cefc51f5aea7c080b1d68bb59b55997d42985c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> are odd, both of these factors are consecutive even numbers, which is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, notice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cefc51f5aea7c080b1d68bb59b55997d42985c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/5733b0696c0ad957576f7fa28b20f46be41baec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv \\pm 1 \\pmod{3} \\implies p^2-1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"334\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059591760b5316f8a1ee60a3adda81e9c8053b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall p \\ge 5, \\, 24 \\mid p^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbaa2d63b4b0621e038e82904fb55f2b59eadbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}\\text{oo}\\vec{\\text{r}}\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Prob